Package: zirt
Title: Zero-Inflated and Hurdle Item Response Models for Scales with
    Filter Questions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Anonymous", "Author", email = "anonymous@example.org",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Marginal maximum likelihood estimation of item response models
    for scales in which most respondents report no symptoms or problems.
    Fits the graded response model, the zero-inflated mixture graded response
    model with a class of structural zeros, and the multidimensional hurdle
    graded response model that separates susceptibility from severity.
    Handles scale-level filter questions, sampling weights and stratified
    cluster designs, and provides model comparison, scoring with posterior
    probabilities of structural zeros, expected score distributions and a
    data generator.
